@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] theme-light-dark-system
Appearance is Light, Dark or System, and the whole app follows it: every page, every
sheet, the window behind them and the launch screen. In dark mode none of them has a
blue or teal cast (rule 76; F13, audit 15 Oct).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] theme-colour-themes
The app offers colour themes in the manner of OpenCode's: a Themes row in Settings and a
Themes command in Commands both open one sheet to pick a theme, and the pick applies at
once to the whole app (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 08:33 to 09:11; K18).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] theme-changes-colours-only
A colour theme replaces colour roles only. Type, shapes, spacing, shadows' geometry,
motion and components are the same under every theme, and every theme defines every
colour role for light and for dark, so no screen falls back to a hard-coded colour.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] theme-material-follows-pulls
The few Material pieces still drawn (menus, dialogs, text selection) read their colours
from the current Pulls palette, so they never show Material's own purple or a colour
that differs from the theme around them.
